License v3.0. See LICENSE.

It includes changes by Nathan Tableman from jay23606/weatherflow-collector
(https://github.com/jay23606/weatherflow-collector): the startup station
metadata retry with a last-good cache, its tests, and the rapid_wind
wind_speed normalization.

Changes in this fork, starting November 2026, are recorded in the git
history. In summary:

- 2026-11: left out a maintenance script with a hard-coded credential;
  removed the export processor, file storage, websocket server provider and
  an unconditional import of a module that was not in the repository;
  updated dependencies for Python 3.13; rebuilt the container image as a
  hardened image on Docker Hardened Images; added tests, CI, signed releases, Dependabot
  and secret scanning.
